# OpenStenoMask — PIO Program for PDM Microphone Capture

This file describes the PIO assembly program needed for PDM mic clocking and data capture. It should be compiled with the Pico SDK's PIO assembler (pioasm).

## pdm_capture.pio

```pio
; PDM Microphone Capture Program
; Clocks a PDM microphone and reads data bits via shift register
; 
; PIO config:
;   - OUT: clock pin (sideset, max 6 pins)
;   - IN:  data pin
;   - Clock divider: system_clock / desired_clock / cycles_per_bit
;
; At 1.024 MHz clock from 133 MHz system:
;   133,000,000 / 1,024,000 / 2 = ~65 (2 cycles per bit)

.program pdm_capture
.side_set 1

.wrap_target
    set pins, 1     side 1      ; Clock high
    nop             side 1      ; Hold clock high (sample at midpoint)
    set pins, 0     side 0      ; Clock low
    in pins, 1      side 0      ; Read data bit into ISR
.wrap

% c-sdk {
#include "hardware/pio.h"

static inline void pdm_capture_program_init(PIO pio, uint sm, uint offset,
                                             uint clk_pin, uint data_pin,
                                             uint32_t clk_hz) {
    pio_gpio_init(pio, clk_pin);
    pio_gpio_init(pio, data_pin);

    pio_sm_set_consecutive_pindirs(pio, sm, clk_pin, 1, true);   /* output */
    pio_sm_set_consecutive_pindirs(pio, sm, data_pin, 1, false);  /* input */

    pio_sm_config c = pdm_capture_program_get_default_config(offset);
    sm_config_set_sideset_pins(&c, clk_pin);
    sm_config_set_in_pins(&c, data_pin);
    sm_config_set_in_shift(&c, false, true, 32);  /* shift right, auto-push at 32 bits */

    /* Clock divider: system_clock / (2 * clk_hz) */
    float div = (float)clock_get_hz(clk_sys) / (2.0f * clk_hz);
    sm_config_set_clkdiv(&c, div);

    pio_sm_init(pio, sm, offset, &c);
}
%}
```

## Build

```bash
# The .pio file is compiled by pioasm (included with Pico SDK)
# Output: pdm_capture.pio.h (auto-generated, included by pdm_capture.c)
```
